                <pb facs="0667" n="617" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg617"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr. Muruaga.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-03-26"><hi rendition="#italic">March 26,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My dear Mr. Minister</hi>: Upon the receipt of your
                    note of yesterday’s date, informing him of an attack by an armed mob on the
                    Spanish cigar makers at Key West, the Secretary at once brought the matter to
                    the attention of the governor of Florida by telegraph for proper action by him.
                    The governor’s reply has just reached us, stating that he has instructed the
                    captain of the company of State troops at Key West to aid the civil authorities
                    in preserving peace.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
